{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VyGmdGrwbPcfadtABS8pDZ","type":"tool_result","content":"paper3:\nETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD\nREADME.md\nlatex\n\npaper3/latex:\nMakefile\nfigures\nmain.pdf\nmain.tex\nrefs.bib\nsec10_conclusion.tex\nsec11_data.tex\nsec12_ack.tex\nsec1_intro.tex\nsec2_statement.tex\nsec3_beyond.tex\nsec4_proof.tex\nsec5_replay.tex\nsec6_consequences.tex\nsec7_practitioner.tex\nsec8_lean.tex\nsec9_related.tex\nsecA_appendix_lean.tex\ntables\n\npaper3/latex/figures:\n\npaper3/latex/tables:\n---MAIN\n% Paper 3 -- skeleton written at the setup of Ralph loop0015 (2026-11-05).\n%\n% Build: `make` in this directory (latexmk -pdf); `make check` fails on any\n% undefined reference or citation. House setup copied from paper1/latex/main.tex\n% (article class, Palatino, natbib plainnat, Appendix A of Lean names).\n%\n% THE TITLE IS FIXED BY THE OWNER AND MUST STAY VERBATIM, INCLUDING THE ELLIPSIS\n% AND THE FINAL PERIOD. The plain string is:\n%   Exponential time hypothesis is false... but the verified algorithm is slower than trying all 2^n assignments at every practical size.\n% In \\title below `$2^n$` and `\\ldots` are its only LaTeX; the pdftitle carries\n% the plain string. The gate (Ralph_Loops/loop0015/gate.py) checks it. Questions\n% about the wording go to ../ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD, never into the title.\n\\documentclass[11pt,letterpaper]{article}\n\n\\usepackage[T1]{fontenc}\n\\usepackage[utf8]{inputenc}\n\\usepackage[sc]{mathpazo}\n\\linespread{1.05}\n\\usepackage{courier}\n\\usepackage[protrusion=true,expansion=false]{microtype}\n\\usepackage[margin=1in]{geometry}\n\\usepackage{amsmath,amssymb,amsthm}\n\\usepackage{graphicx}\n\\usepackage{booktabs}\n\\usepackage{array}\n\\usepackage{tabularx}\n\\usepackage{longtable}\n\\usepackage{caption}\n\\usepackage{float}\n\\usepackage[section]{placeins}\n\\usepackage{xcolor}\n\\usepackage[hyphens]{url}\n\\usepackage[title,titletoc]{appendix}\n\\usepackage[authoryear,round]{natbib}\n\\usepackage[colorlinks=true,linkcolor=blue!50!black,citecolor=blue!50!black,urlcolor=blue!50!black]{hyperref}\n\\hypersetup{pdftitle={Exponential time hypothesis is false... but the verified algorithm is slower than trying all 2\\string^n assignments at every practical size.}}\n\n\\graphicspath{{figures/}}\n\\numberwithin{figure}{section}\n\\numberwithin{table}{section}\n\\captionsetup{font=small,labelfont=bf}\n\\bibliographystyle{plainnat}\n\n% Lean names live in Appendix A (secA_appendix_lean.tex), one entry per\n% result, as in paper 1: \\leanentry{key}{result} opens a row, \\leannames{a, b}\n% prints the names, and the text cites an entry with \\leanref{key}.\n\\makeatletter\n\\g@addto@macro{\\UrlBreaks}{\\do\\_\\do\\.}\n\\newcommand{\\leannames}[1]{\\def\\lean@sep{}\\@for\\lean@n:=#1\\do{\\lean@sep\\expandafter\\path\\expandafter{\\lean@n}\\def\\lean@sep{, }}}\n\\makeatother\n\\newcounter{leanentry}\n\\renewcommand{\\theleanentry}{A.\\arabic{leanentry}}\n\\newcommand{\\leanentry}[2]{\\leavevmode\\refstepcounter{leanentry}\\label{lean:#1}\\theleanentry & #2 &}\n\\newcommand{\\leangroup}[1]{\\multicolumn{3}{@{}l}{\\emph{#1}}\\\\}\n\\newcommand{\\leanref}[1]{(Appendix~\\ref{app:lean}, \\ref{lean:#1})}\n\n\\theoremstyle{plain}\n\\newtheorem{theorem}{Theorem}[section]\n\\newtheorem{lemma}[theorem]{Lemma}\n\\newtheorem{proposition}[theorem]{Proposition}\n\\newtheorem{corollary}[theorem]{Corollary}\n\\theoremstyle{definition}\n\\newtheorem{definition}[theorem]{Definition}\n\\theoremstyle{remark}\n\\newtheorem*{remark}{Remark}\n\n% The verified exponent, rho(n) = n (ln ln(n+16))^2 / sqrt(ln(n+16)), and the\n% comparator's names, used throughout.\n\\newcommand{\\rhon}{\\rho(n)}\n\\newcommand{\\runtimeScale}{\\texttt{runtimeScale}}\n\\newcommand{\\SubexpCount}{\\texttt{SubexpCount}}\n% Paths in the repository and in the clone; a placeholder box for text an item\n% still owes, as in paper 1.\n\\newcommand{\\repofile}[1]{\\path{#1}}\n\\newcommand{\\clonefile}[1]{\\path{#1}}\n\\newcommand{\\placeholder}[1]{\\par\\noindent\\fbox{\\parbox{\\dimexpr\\linewidth-2\\fboxsep-2\\fboxrule}{\\textbf{Placeholder.} #1}}\\par}\n\n% Title: fixed by the owner, verbatim (see the comment at the top).\n\\title{Exponential time hypothesis is false\\ldots{} but the verified algorithm is slower than trying all $2^n$ assignments at every practical size.}\n% Second author is a placeholder to be resolved by the owner (ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD, entry S1).\n\\author{Alexandre Linhares \\and the MOSP project}\n\\date{\\today}\n\n\\begin{document}\n\\maketitle\n\n\\begin{abstract}\n\\noindent\n\\placeholder{Item 09 writes the abstract (under 200 words; no number without a\nsection that regenerates it). The title's sentence made precise: what is\nverified is a guarantee with existential constants and the exponent\n$n(\\log\\log n)^2/\\sqrt{\\log n}$, whose factor exceeds $1$ for every\n$50 \\le n < e^{5504}$, so the verified guarantee is weaker than the trivial\n$2^n \\cdot \\mathrm{poly}$ guarantee at every practical size; the machine's\nrunning time is unknown because the constants are never computed; the\nmanuscript's sharper exponents are unverified; the statement does refute\nETH; the audit found no flaw.}\n\\end{abstract}\n\n\\input{sec1_intro}\n\\input{sec2_statement}\n\\input{sec3_beyond}\n\\input{sec4_proof}\n\\input{sec5_replay}\n\\input{sec6_consequences}\n\\input{sec7_practitioner}\n\\input{sec8_lean}\n\\input{sec9_related}\n\\input{sec10_conclusion}\n\\input{sec11_data}\n\\input{sec12_ack}\n\n\\bibliography{refs}\n\n\\begin{appendices}\n\\input{secA_appendix_lean}\n\\end{appendices}\n\n\\end{document}\n---SEC5\n% Independent replay -- drafted by loop0015 item 01.\n\\section{Independent replay}\n\\label{sec:replay}\n\n\\placeholder{Item 01 drafts this section: the sandboxed build of the SubexponentialSAT closure from a fresh copy of the clone, the \\texttt{\\#print axioms} output, the Lean and Mathlib versions, the time, the hashes of the logs, and whether nanoda ran. Ends with what this does not claim''.}\n---GITIGNORE\n# Paper 3: the sandboxed replay's full logs are large and regenerable; their\n# hashes and the short extracts (axioms.txt, versions, the last 200 lines)\n# are committed by item 01.\nreplay/logs/*.log\nreplay/logs/*.jsonl\nreplay/logs/*.export\nreplay/logs/*.out\n# LaTeX build products (main.pdf is committed, as paper 1's is)\nlatex/*.aux\nlatex/*.bbl\nlatex/*.blg\nlatex/*.fdb_latexmk\nlatex/*.fls\nlatex/*.log\nlatex/*.out\nlatex/*.toc\nlatex/*.synctex.gz\n---README\nExponential time hypothesis is false... but the verified algorithm is slower than trying all 2^n assignments at every practical size.\n\n*(The title above is fixed by the owner and is used verbatim, including\nthe ellipsis and the final period, everywhere: here, in `latex/main.tex`,\nin `reports/paper3_plan.md`, in `Ralph_Loops/loop0015/TASK.md` and in\nevery commit the loop makes. Questions about its wording go to\n`ETH_AMBIGUOUS.MD`, never into the title.)*\n\n**This paper is about the limitation of the ETH refutation and nothing\nelse.** It is not concerned with graphs, pathwidth, treewidth, MOSP or any\nwidth parameter.\n\n## What the paper is\n\nA reading of OpenAI's family 378, *The Exponential Time Hypothesis is\nFalse* (`github.com/openai/math`, 2026-10-25; cloned read-only under\n`~/dev/untrusted/openai-math`, commit `4eaee875`), by people who checked:\n\n- **what the Lean-verified statement says exactly** (`lean/ComparatorChallenges/SubexponentialSAT.lean`\n  in the clone): for each `k ≥ 2` there *exist* a finite multitape machine\n  and constants `C, A, S, d, e` such that on every width-`≤ k` CNF, in a\n  canonical encoding of bit length `L`, the machine halts with the exact\n  count within `C (L + 1)^d · 2^{A · ρ(n)}` steps,\n  `ρ(n) = n (ln ln(n + 16))² / √ln(n + 16)`. A **guarantee**, not a\n  running time; the constants are never computed; the exponent is `ρ(n)`\n  only — the manuscript's sharper `n log log n / √log n` and `n / √log n`\n  are not in the Lean library. The factor `ρ(n)/n` exceeds 1 for every\n  `50 ≤ n < e^{5504}` (peak `16/e² ≈ 2.17` near `n ≈ 10^{23.7}`), so with\n  `A = 1` the verified bound is above `2^n` at every practical size: the\n  verified guarantee is weaker than the trivial `2^n · poly` guarantee of\n  trying all assignments. The statement does refute ETH as stated.\n- **an independent inspection and replay of the proof**: the closure of\n  3,091 modules with no `axiom`, `sorry`, `native_decide`,\n  `implemented_by`, `unsafe` or `partial`, 33 statement definitions\n  identical to the comparator's, the compile lemmas concluding in the\n  comparator's own `Trace`; and (item 01) a build of that closure in an\n  isolated `bwrap` sandbox with `#print axioms` recorded, since the\n  repository holds no recorded axiom audit, no CI and no second-kernel\n  (nanoda) replay for this family.\n- **what follows**: ETH, SETH, Gap-ETH, #ETH and their randomised forms\n  refuted as the statement supports; lower bounds derived from them lose\n  their premise while the statements they concluded are not themselves\n  refuted (the manuscript's own §1.1.3).\n- **what it changes for a practitioner**: nothing on any machine — a\n  measurement of a SAT solver and a model counter on random 3-CNF against\n  `2^{ρ(n)}` and `2^n`.\n\nThe two audits the paper rests on are `reports/scratch/eth_audit/\nstatement_audit.md` and `proof_audit.md` (2026-11-05). The plan is\n`reports/paper3_plan.md`; the loop that writes the paper is\n`Ralph_Loops/loop0015/`.\n\n## Layout\n\n| path | content |\n|---|---|\n| `latex/` | the paper: `main.tex` (title verbatim, abstract, section inputs), `sec*.tex`, `refs.bib`, `Makefile` (`make`, `make check`), `figures/`, `tables/` |\n| `scripts/` | every number's regenerate script (`runtime_scale.py`, `practitioner.py`, …), written by the items |\n| `replay/` | the sandboxed replay: `README.md` with the exact commands, `logs/` (full logs git-ignored, hashes committed) 