{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PMoy1dimfzsbJ8Wbv4K5S2","type":"tool_result","content":"Yes, the README names nanoda, external kernels, and `enable_nanoda`.\n\n**Nanoda and external kernels**\n- \"Comparator can additionally check solutions with external kernels.\"\n- \"This is only necessary if you want to check with the nanoda kernel in addition to the builtin one.\"\n- \"`cargo build --release` will place `nanoda_bin` in the `target/release` directory\"\n- \"`COMPARATOR_LANDRUN`, `COMPARATOR_LEAN4EXPORT`, and `COMPARATOR_NANODA` when invoking Comparator.\"\n- \"For backwards compatibility reasons users may instead set `enable_nanoda: true` to obtain a config that calls `nanoda_bin`.\"\n- \"Furthermore, comparator currently attempts to detect `nanoda`-style kernels by checking whether the name contains\"\n- \"For development purposes, comparator supports overriding `nanoda` specifically\"\n- \"The Lean kernel is correct (with `external_kernels` this can be reduced to\"\n\n**lean4export**\n- \"at a version that is compatible with whatever Lean version your project is targeting, present in `PATH`\"\n- \"Run `lean4export` on the produced `Challenge.olean` in a `landrun` sandbox that has:\"\n\n**Permitted axioms**\n- \"Use no more axioms than listed in `permitted_axioms`\"\n- \"Verify that the body of all relevant theorems in the `Solution` environment only uses axioms listed in `permitted_axioms`\"\n\n**Sandbox (landrun)**\n- \"compiled from the `main` branch's source, present in `PATH`\"\n- \"`landrun` works correctly on your system and `Solution.lean` does not exploit any bugs in `landrun`\"\n- \"Build `Challenge` using `lake` in a `landrun` sandbox that has:\"\n- \"The systemd-run part explicitly guard against a vulnerability in landrun, Comparator's current sandboxing solution\"\n- \"The `scripts/fake-landrun.sh` can be used to replace Landrun in development\"\n\n**What comparator checks**\n\nThe README says that for theorems listed in `theorem_names`, the solution is guaranteed to:\n- \"Prove the same statement as provided in `Challenge`\"\n- \"Use no more axioms than listed in `permitted_axioms`\"\n- \"Be accepted by the Lean kernel\"\n\nFor definition holes (`definition_names`), it also checks that \"The name, type, universe levels and safety levels of all definition holes match.\" The README adds that definition-hole solutions \"must always be checked with an additional (potentially human) verifier.\""}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e952065-9d21-48cd-9ba0-35babc908345","uuid":"8e08c7f5-a9be-4789-88fa-bd38e6f09fe6","timestamp":"2026-11-05T01:31:17.166Z","tool_use_result":{"bytes":282790,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"Yes, the README names nanoda, external kernels, and `enable_nanoda`.\n\n**Nanoda and external kernels**\n- \"Comparator can additionally check solutions with external kernels.\"\n- \"This is only necessary if you want to check with the nanoda kernel in addition to the builtin one.\"\n- \"`cargo build --release` will place `nanoda_bin` in the `target/release` directory\"\n- \"`COMPARATOR_LANDRUN`, `COMPARATOR_LEAN4EXPORT`, and `COMPARATOR_NANODA` when invoking Comparator.\"\n- \"For backwards compatibility reasons users may instead set `enable_nanoda: true` to obtain a config that calls `nanoda_bin`.\"\n- \"Furthermore, comparator currently attempts to detect `nanoda`-style kernels by checking whether the name contains\"\n- \"For development purposes, comparator supports overriding `nanoda` specifically\"\n- \"The Lean kernel is correct (with `external_kernels` this can be reduced to\"\n\n**lean4export**\n- \"at a version that is compatible with whatever Lean version your project is targeting, present in `PATH`\"\n- \"Run `lean4export` on the produced `Challenge.olean` in a `landrun` sandbox that has:\"\n\n**Permitted axioms**\n- \"Use no more axioms than listed in `permitted_axioms`\"\n- \"Verify that the body of all relevant theorems in the `Solution` environment only uses axioms listed in `permitted_axioms`\"\n\n**Sandbox (landrun)**\n- \"compiled from the `main` branch's source, present in `PATH`\"\n- \"`landrun` works correctly on your system and `Solution.lean` does not exploit any bugs in `landrun`\"\n- \"Build `Challenge` using `lake` in a `landrun` sandbox that has:\"\n- \"The systemd-run part explicitly guard against a vulnerability in landrun, Comparator's current sandboxing solution\"\n- \"The `scripts/fake-landrun.sh` can be used to replace Landrun in development\"\n\n**What comparator checks**\n\nThe README says that for theorems listed in `theorem_names`, the solution is guaranteed to:\n- \"Prove the same statement as provided in `Challenge`\"\n- \"Use no more axioms than listed in `permitted_axioms`\"\n- \"Be accepted by the Lean kernel\"\n\nFor definition holes (`definition_names`), it also checks that \"The name, type, universe levels and safety levels of all definition holes match.\" The README adds that definition-hole solutions \"must always be checked with an additional (potentially human) verifier.\"","durationMs":18781,"url":"https://github.com/leanprover/comparator"},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01PMoy1dimfzsbJ8Wbv4K5S2","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
