{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011Cgiv7s9LYRySbCxCCt4vn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01GSMxEpfmR73pJf8fVHPxoC","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > paper3/latex/sec5_replay.tex <<'EOF'\n% Independent replay -- drafted by loop0015 item 01 (2026-11-05).\n% Every number here is read from paper3/replay/logs/ (regenerate: re-run\n% ~/dev/untrusted/replay/run_sandbox.sh as paper3/replay/README.md records;\n% the counts below come from `grep -c` on the copied logs, see\n% paper3/replay/logs/run2/counts.txt).\n\\section{Independent replay}\n\\label{sec:replay}\n\nThe repository holds no recorded \\texttt{\\#print axioms} output for the\nfamily, no continuous integration that builds its Lean, and\n\\texttt{enable\\_nanoda: false} in the comparator's JSON\n(Section~\\ref{sec:proof}). We therefore built the solution's import\nclosure ourselves, in isolation, at the toolchain the repository pins, and\nrecorded what the kernel reports. This section says exactly what was run,\nwhere, and what came out; the scripts are quoted verbatim in\n\\repofile{paper3/replay/README.md}, and the logs are under\n\\repofile{paper3/replay/logs/}.\n\n\\subsection{What was run, and where}\n\nA fresh copy of the clone (commit \\texttt{4eaee875}) was built inside a\n\\texttt{bwrap} (bubblewrap) sandbox on the project's machine: the system\ndirectories bound read-only, a private \\texttt{tmpfs} home with nothing of\nthe real home or of this repository visible, separate PID, IPC and UTS\nnamespaces, the whole sandbox confined to eight cores\n(\\texttt{taskset -c 0-7}) at the lowest scheduling priority, and the\nnetwork on, because the repository's \\texttt{lakefile} clones its 41\ndependencies at build time and the Mathlib object files come from the\nMathlib cache. Inside, \\texttt{elan} was installed into the private home\nand fetched the pinned toolchain from the repository's own\n\\texttt{lean-toolchain} file; then, in the clone's \\texttt{lean/}\ndirectory, \\texttt{lake exe cache get}, \\texttt{lake build\nOAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Main} (the solution's closure, not the\ncollection's default target, which builds all 721 families), and\n\\texttt{\\#print axioms} of the one theorem the comparator names,\n\\texttt{OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace.exact\\_count\\_and\\_sat},\nthrough \\texttt{lake env lean}. Only text left the sandbox; nothing built\ninside it was executed outside it.\n\nTwo runs were needed. The first, started at 01:03 on 2026-11-05, failed\nat once at the build step because its command line carried \\texttt{-j 8},\nan option this version of Lake does not have (the whole of its build log\nis the one line \\texttt{error: unknown short option '-j'}); nothing of\nthe family was compiled. The second, started at 01:16 with that option\nremoved and the core cap moved to \\texttt{taskset}, is the run reported\nbelow. Both scripts, both versions, and the launch command are in the\nREADME; the first run's logs are kept beside the second's.\n\n\\subsection{What came out}\n\nREPLAY_RESULTS\n\n\\subsection{The second kernel}\n\nNANODA_RESULTS\n\n\\subsection{What this does not claim}\n\n\\begin{itemize}\n\\item The replay trusts the Lean kernel of the pinned toolchain\n  (\\texttt{v4.34.1}) and upstream Mathlib at the pinned revision; it\n  moves the proof's trust from ``OpenAI's unpublished build'' to ``a\n  build we ran'', not from the Lean kernel to anything else.\n  NANODA_CLAIM\n\\item It is not the comparator run. The comparator checks that the\n  solution's exported statement matches the challenge's by\n  \\texttt{lean4export}; we did not run that tool chain, and the\n  statement-level match the paper relies on is the textual one of\n  Section~\\ref{sec:proof} (the 33 definitions and the theorem statement,\n  identical character for character after whitespace normalisation).\n\\item The counts above are counts of lines in one build's log on one\n  machine with the named versions; a different Lake would print different\n  job totals (the 12,014 includes the cached Mathlib modules), and a\n  different machine a different time.\n\\item Nothing here bears on what the theorem \\emph{says}\n  (Section~\\ref{sec:statement}) or on the manuscript's unverified\n  exponents (Section~\\ref{sec:beyond}); a replayed proof of a weak bound\n  is a replayed proof of a weak bound.\n\\end{itemize}\nEOF\necho written","description":"Draft the replay section with result markers"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":948,"cache_read_input_tokens":163823,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":948,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e952065-9d21-48cd-9ba0-35babc908345","uuid":"e775a8ca-86b6-4b7e-94ad-581041734b0c","timestamp":"2026-11-05T01:31:21.830Z","request_id":"req_011Cgiv7rp11MMVug5S9J1pQ","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01GSMxEpfmR73pJf8fVHPxoC":{"command":"cd /home/al/dev/MOSP && cat > paper3/latex/sec5_replay.tex <<'EOF'\n% Independent replay -- drafted by loop0015 item 01 (2026-11-05).\n% Every number here is read from paper3/replay/logs/ (regenerate: re-run\n% ~/dev/untrusted/replay/run_sandbox.sh as paper3/replay/README.md records;\n% the counts below come from `grep -c` on the copied logs, see\n% paper3/replay/logs/run2/counts.txt).\n\\section{Independent replay}\n\\label{sec:replay}\n\nThe repository holds no recorded \\texttt{\\#print axioms} output for the\nfamily, no continuous integration that builds its Lean, and\n\\texttt{enable\\_nanoda: false} in the comparator's JSON\n(Section~\\ref{sec:proof}). We therefore built the solution's import\nclosure ourselves, in isolation, at the toolcha