{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GSMxEpfmR73pJf8fVHPxoC","type":"tool_result","content":"written","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5e952065-9d21-48cd-9ba0-35babc908345","uuid":"692c25d1-1df8-4925-91b5-250b5b9a03af","timestamp":"2026-11-05T01:41:17.516Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"written","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/latex/sec5_replay.tex","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":5,"newStart":1,"newLines":79,"lines":["-% Independent replay -- drafted by loop0015 item 01.","+% Independent replay -- drafted by loop0015 item 01 (2026-11-05).","+% Every number here is read from paper3/replay/logs/ (regenerate: re-run","+% ~/dev/untrusted/replay/run_sandbox.sh as paper3/replay/README.md records;","+% the counts below come from `grep -c` on the copied logs, see","+% paper3/replay/logs/run2/counts.txt)."," \\section{Independent replay}"," \\label{sec:replay}"," ","-\\placeholder{Item 01 drafts this section: the sandboxed build of the SubexponentialSAT closure from a fresh copy of the clone, the \\texttt{\\#print axioms} output, the Lean and Mathlib versions, the time, the hashes of the logs, and whether nanoda ran. Ends with what this does not claim''.}","+The repository holds no recorded \\texttt{\\#print axioms} output for the","+family, no continuous integration that builds its Lean, and","+\\texttt{enable\\_nanoda: false} in the comparator's JSON","+(Section~\\ref{sec:proof}). We therefore built the solution's import","+closure ourselves, in isolation, at the toolchain the repository pins, and","+recorded what the kernel reports. This section says exactly what was run,","+where, and what came out; the scripts are quoted verbatim in","+\\repofile{paper3/replay/README.md}, and the logs are under","+\\repofile{paper3/replay/logs/}.","+","+\\subsection{What was run, and where}","+","+A fresh copy of the clone (commit \\texttt{4eaee875}) was built inside a","+\\texttt{bwrap} (bubblewrap) sandbox on the project's machine: the system","+directories bound read-only, a private \\texttt{tmpfs} home with nothing of","+the real home or of this repository visible, separate PID, IPC and UTS","+namespaces, the whole sandbox confined to eight cores","+(\\texttt{taskset -c 0-7}) at the lowest scheduling priority, and the","+network on, because the repository's \\texttt{lakefile} clones its 41","+dependencies at build time and the Mathlib object files come from the","+Mathlib cache. Inside, \\texttt{elan} was installed into the private home","+and fetched the pinned toolchain from the repository's own","+\\texttt{lean-toolchain} file; then, in the clone's \\texttt{lean/}","+directory, \\texttt{lake exe cache get}, \\texttt{lake build","+OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.Main} (the solution's closure, not the","+collection's default target, which builds all 721 families), and","+\\texttt{\\#print axioms} of the one theorem the comparator names,","+\\texttt{OAI.Algorithms.SubexponentialSAT.SqrtLogSpace.exact\\_count\\_and\\_sat},","+through \\texttt{lake env lean}. Only text left the sandbox; nothing built","+inside it was executed outside it.","+","+Two runs were needed. The first, started at 01:03 on 2026-11-05, failed","+at once at the build step because its command line carried \\texttt{-j 8},","+an option this version of Lake does not have (the whole of its build log","+is the one line \\texttt{error: unknown short option '-j'}); nothing of","+the family was compiled. The second, started at 01:16 with that option","+removed and the core cap moved to \\texttt{taskset}, is the run reported","+below. Both scripts, both versions, and the launch command are in the","+README; the first run's logs are kept beside the second's.","+","+\\subsection{What came out}","+","+REPLAY_RESULTS","+","+\\subsection{The second kernel}","+","+NANODA_RESULTS","+","+\\subsection{What this does not claim}","+","+\\begin{itemize}","+\\item The replay trusts the Lean kernel of the pinned toolchain","+  (\\texttt{v4.34.1}) and upstream Mathlib at the pinned revision; it","+  moves the proof's trust from ``OpenAI's unpublished build'' to ``a","+  build we ran'', not from the Lean kernel to anything else.","+  NANODA_CLAIM","+\\item It is not the comparator run. The comparator checks that the","+  solution's exported statement matches the challenge's by","+  \\texttt{lean4export}; we did not run that tool chain, and the","+  statement-level match the paper relies on is the textual one of","+  Section~\\ref{sec:proof} (the 33 definitions and the theorem statement,","+  identical character for character after whitespace normalisation).","+\\item The counts above are counts of lines in one build's log on one","+  machine with the named versions; a different Lake would print different","+  job totals (the 12,014 includes the cached Mathlib modules), and a","+  different machine a different time.","+\\item Nothing here bears on what the theorem \\emph{says}","+  (Section~\\ref{sec:statement}) or on the manuscript's unverified","+  exponents (Section~\\ref{sec:beyond}); a replayed proof of a weak bound","+  is a replayed proof of a weak bound.","+\\end{itemize}"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/paper3/latex/sec5_replay.tex"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01GSMxEpfmR73pJf8fVHPxoC","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
